    "intro_html":  "Ca ri ga is Vietnam\u0027s curry, and it sits in its own lane. Lemongrass and coconut milk give it perfume, potato and sweet potato give it body, and it is seasoned with fish sauce rather than the spice cabinet, which is why it tastes lighter and more soup-like than the Indian and Thai curries on this site. It is traditionally eaten with a baguette for dipping, which tells you everything about Vietnam\u0027s history in one detail. Each bowl runs \u003cstrong\u003e708 calories and 27 grams of protein\u003c/strong\u003e for about \u003cstrong\u003e$4.90\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost).",
